     We next prove \eqref{P2} by utilizing Tchakaloff's theorem (see e.g., \cite{Tchakaloff}) to show the existence of a cubature rule for the integration of polynomials, i.e., there exist $\{(\mathbf{x}_j,w_j): 1 \leq j \leq N := k + {\rm deg} (K) \} \subset \mathcal{X} \times \mathbb{R}_{>0}$ 
