    \nonumber \\
    &\leq &  2^{m-1}\binom{k+m-1}{m-1}\left(\sum_{i=1}^m c(n_i,k)\right)\frac{1}{r^2}.
    \label{eq-lambda-bound}
\end{eqnarray}
Here, the coefficient $2^{m-1}$ comes from the fact that $\lambda^{(i)}_j \in [1/2,1]$, the coefficient $\binom{k+m-1}{m-1}$ is the result of counting the tuple $(j_1,\dots,j_{i-1},j_{i+1},\dots,j_m)$ such that $\sum_{i=1}^mj_i \leq k$, and the last inequality is based on Lemma~\ref{lemma: recall results}.
In short, we can obtain the following inequality:
\begin{displaymath}
